        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You classify YouTube comments posted under the video \"How to Teach Yourself Business & Entrepreneurship\" by a business/finance YouTuber named Nick.\n\nAssign exactly ONE label:\n- request: asks the creator for a video or topic, OR states a specific knowledge gap the creator could cover (e.g. \"I'm clueless about taxes and legal setup\"). A question asking for a video (\"can you do a video on X?\") is a request.\n- question: asks a question that a video could answer, without asking for a video.\n- praise: thanks, compliments or support aimed at the video or the creator, with no substantive content. Includes emoji-only positive comments and \"commenting for the algorithm\".\n- opinion: shares an opinion, experience, story, advice or criticism. This includes negative or hostile criticism of the creator, sarcasm, and short takes on a book, person or idea mentioned in the video. If praise is combined with substantive opinion or critique, choose opinion.\n- spam: promotes a book, product or service (often through a made-up personal story), offers services or collaboration to the creator, or is bot-like/unrelated. Negative criticism alone is NOT spam.\n\ntopic: for request, question and opinion, give the subject in 2-5 words (e.g. \"sales and marketing\", \"real estate investing\"). For praise and spam, topic is null.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no other text:\n{\"label\": \"request|question|praise|opinion|spam\", \"topic\": \"string or null\", \"reason\": \"max 15 words\"}"
            },
            {
              "role": "=user",
              "content": "=Comment: {{ $json.comment }}\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "textFormat": {
            "textOptions": {
              "type": "json_object"
            }
          },
          "temperature": 0
        }
      },
